<Base title="Vehicle transport condition — How It Was" description="Walk around your vehicle and document its condition before collection.">
  <section class="product-hero wrap"><div class="product-copy"><span class="section-index">VEHICLE TRANSPORT / WALKTHROUGH</span><h1>Before the keys<br/><span>change hands.</span></h1><p class="lead">Your car is going on a transporter. Take a few minutes to photograph its condition before it leaves your sight.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/vehicle-transport/capture/">Start the walkthrough <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="microcopy">Free local draft · No account · Optional online record</p></div><div class="product-photo"><img src="/vehicle-hero.webp" alt="Silver-blue vehicle before collection" width="1672" height="941"/><div class="product-photo-label"><span>YOUR WALKAROUND</span><strong>8 guided exterior views</strong></div></div></section>
  <section class="section wrap before-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-index">BEFORE YOU START</span><h2>Have your vehicle nearby.</h2></div><p>Good light helps. Include the whole vehicle in each exterior photo, then take close-ups of marks you want to note. Do this as close to collection as practical.</p></div><div class="prep-grid"><div><span>01</span><strong>Add the details</strong><p>Registration, make and model, plus collection information.</p></div><div><span>02</span><strong>Walk around the car</strong><p>Eight prompts guide you from the front around to the other side.</p></div><div><span>03</span><strong>Note existing marks</strong><p>Add close-ups and descriptions, then review your local draft.</p></div></div><div class="honesty-box"><div class="honesty-icon">i</div><div><strong>About the record</strong><p>The free draft stays in this browser. If you choose online storage at checkout, original photos are uploaded to a private record with a server receipt and integrity digest. Those do not independently verify when or where a photo was taken. Keep your original photos separately.</p></div></div></section>
</Base>
